{
  "id": "bigville_will",
  "version": "1.3.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R54 (block 365000): a WILL IS A NOTE that says what to do when you die -- not a special object, and not auto-distributed. Any Note (the same kind agents write/hold/give/relay, bigville_noticeboard) that names a testator (-willed_by-> dead), an EXECUTOR (-executor-> agent), and bequests (-bequeaths-> Bequest{amount} -to-> beneficiary) is a will. On the testator's death, once BURIED (funeral fee already taken -- bigville_cemetery), the EXECUTOR reads the note and DECIDES: wl_decide collapses {honour, withhold} valued by honesty - greed. wl_honour: he enacts each bequest (pays the beneficiary from the estate; abatement if short). wl_withhold: a grasping executor keeps the estate for himself (a betrayal, contestable via the court). The estate flows ONLY because an agent decided to enact the wishes -- NOT automatically. wl_intestate: no will-note -> the next of kin takes the estate. Composes with the NOTE machinery (a will is written, held, given, relayed like any note), bigville_cemetery (funeral first), ownership/estate/coin, the court/theft (contesting a withholding executor), and bigville_office (the executor is a duty/role). v1.3.0: PIOUS BEQUESTS -- the testator DECIDES whether to leave some money to the church -- pl_pious_decide is a COLLAPSE {bequeath, keep} valued by the agent's OWN piety - greed (from its graph, NOT a threshold), so the pious give (even the poor) and the worldly keep it; pl_pious_grant writes the church legacy (piety*gift_rate, abated to the estate). The church receives pious legacies when the executor honours the will.",
